{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Vanessa and the Customer Complaint", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Panic in the Kitchen", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 2, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Dealing with Customers", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When things go wrong when you are at work, you can talk about the problems using : <span class=\"italic\">should</span>, <span class=\"italic\">should not</span> and <span class=\"italic\">supposed to</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use also use <span class=\"italic\">supposed to</span> when you apologize. <br/> You add <span class=\"italic\">not</span> to firmly explain the problem wasn't because of you.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">This should not happen.<br/><br/>  Tanya is supposed to be in charge of cheesecakes.<br/><br/>  Daniel was supposed to finish them.<br/><br/>  It's supposed to be sugar not salt. <br/><br/>  This bag should be sugar. <br/><br/>  We're never supposed to taste the dessert batters.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It's not expected.<br/><br/>   She was not in charge today.<br/><br/>   Perhaps he did this.<br/><br/>   It's not as it should be.<br/><br/>  I expected something else.<br/><br/>  It's unacceptable.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Discuss How to Deal with Problems", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When you deal with problems you can use modals like: <span class=\"italic\">have to</span>, <span class=\"italic\">had better</span>, <span class=\"italic\">ought to</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">might want to</span>, for what is advisable.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use the modals to show what is necessary or advisable to do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I'd better talk to him.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Daniel, you had better have a good explanation for this.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We have to get in touch with the supplier! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "They'll have to check their supplies.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You'd better come with me. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We have to explain this.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "However, after this I guess you ought to at least taste the sugar.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to be in charge of", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be responsible for", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Tanya is supposed to be in charge of cheesecakes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about problems in the kitchen.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to go through", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to look at and check", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I went through all of the pies, cakes and cheesecakes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to affect", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to cause a change in", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This is the only one affected.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "explanation", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a reason for", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Daniel, you had better have a good explanation for this. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "fault", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something you are to blame for", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I am very sorry but it's not my fault.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "clearly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "obviously", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can see it's clearly marked.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to mark", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to write", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The name is marked on the bag.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le02ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Tell your teacher about homework you were supposed to do but did not do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Explain why you did not do it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a letter to your teacher apologizing for your mistake. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use had better/should to explain what you will do next time you have the same problem.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read the letter to a friend.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about something I am supposed to do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write a letter apologizing for not doing it.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about how I will deal with the problem next time.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "sch